# Experiment 3 - ER Diagram

## Aim

To design an Entity Relationship Diagram for a College Database System.

## Entities

### Student

Attributes:

- student_id
- student_name
- email
- department

### Course

Attributes:

- course_id
- course_name
- credits

### Faculty

Attributes:

- faculty_id
- faculty_name
- department

## Relationships

Student enrolls in Course.

Faculty teaches Course.

## Relationship Structure

Student
↓
Enrolls
↓
Course

Faculty
↓
Teaches
↓
Course

## Cardinality

A student can enroll in many courses.

A course can contain many students.

Therefore:

Student ↔ Course

is a Many-to-Many relationship.

A faculty member can teach multiple courses.

## Conclusion

ER diagrams help us visually understand entities, attributes and relationships before creating database tables.
